<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Hicor 15-month results.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Hicor 15-month results.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>15 months to March 31, 1997 vs 12 months to December 31, 1995</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		 4.0	   vs 5.0</p>
<p>    Net income		5.61	  vs 5.59</p>
<p>    Outside shareholders' 3.08	  vs 2.64</p>
<p>    Retained income	 2.53	  vs 2.95</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   9.75	  vs 7.89</p>
<p>    Tax			 4.14	  vs 2.30</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   5.16	  vs 1.43</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    3.93	  vs 1.99</p>
<p>    Turnover		  216.84	vs 139.64</p>
<p>Full name: Hicor Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it had changed its year end to reflect the full cyclical nature of its operations. This however had a negative effect on earnings for both the clothing and electronic operations as January to March is traditionally the worst trading quarter. Net operating income was also hit by a bad debt write-off of 950,0000 rand and a stock write-off of 2.2 million.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
